# Unpublished model version history prototype

This isolated OpenAPI 3.1 / v1 candidate changes no product contract or route.
It reuses the existing immutable model-version ID, catalogs and dataset-lineage
shapes. Family UUIDs in tests are explicit synthetic owner inputs, never inferred
from a name, model_key, catalog digest or derivation parent.

The list is a bounded metadata page; the separate historical detail admits ready
and retired metadata. Existing ready-only ModelVersion and Portal/list shapes remain unchanged.
The prototype Admin detail adds one optional owner-supplied family_id; old
responses may omit it and remain valid. Deployment and training continue to select the exact
immutable version ID and must run their original admission.

The model-owner-decisions.json file lists domain inputs required before a public
contract or storage/route implementation is finalized. No ordinal version number,
family backfill, execution permission, second lineage store or route success is
invented here. The owner must provide durable membership, current scope and
retained graph reads. Prototype SDK generation and wire receipts are separate
from real PostgreSQL, dispatcher and S-202 qualification.
